  "body": "Hi 👋\nI was wondering if there’s a specific reason why, when a RAW image is processed with the Neutral profile via the CLI, the ARP ends up with the default temperature and tint values. Would it make sense to write the computed values instead?\n\nIn my case, I opened a RAW file in the GUI and set the Neutral profile. When switching to Camera, it correctly sets the computed values. However, when preprocessing with the CLI using -O, the output sidecar still contains the default values.\n\nDo you think it would make sense to write the computed values in this case as well? I’d love to hear your thoughts. Thanks in advance, appreciate the help 🙌",
